# Campaign YAML

- Keep `metadata.id: devops-dungeon` and five `order`ed rooms. Seats stay cosmetic.
- `story.clues` are lobby-map chests (overworld `x` / `y`). Room `clues` stay on that room. Unique `id`s across both.
- Every room: `puzzle_type`, `expected_command_pattern`, `accepted_examples`, `forbidden_patterns` (when there is a cursed form), `hint`, `narrative`, `success_narrative`, `canvas_event`.
- Win conditions live in regex + examples, never only in `game_master.system_prompt`.
- Boss `requires_loot`: `rune-thorn`, `rune-ash`, `rune-oak`, `rune-iron`.
- `puzzle_type` is `linux` | `ansible` | `openshift` | `java` only.
- After edits, sync engine classpath copy and gitops ConfigMap; restart the engine (no reload route).
- Quality: `./verify.sh` (yamllint, ruff, pytest-cov). Never put Hugging Face tokens, kubeconfigs, or API keys in YAML.
